cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rob2-kit, please cite it as below."
title: "rob2-kit: evidence-grounded Cochrane RoB 2 assessment with AI agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Salman
    given-names: Ali
version: 0.12.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AliSalman-et-al/rob2-kit"
abstract: >-
  rob2-kit is a model-free Model Context Protocol server and agent skill for
  Cochrane Risk of Bias 2 (RoB 2) assessment of randomized trials. An AI agent
  reads the trial reports and answers the signalling questions with cited
  passages. The server validates each citation against the captured sources,
  applies the official RoB 2 algorithms deterministically, keeps the researcher
  as the approver of the assessed result, and exports a verifiable bundle.
keywords:
  - risk of bias
  - RoB 2
  - Cochrane
  - systematic review
  - randomized controlled trials
  - large language models
  - Model Context Protocol
references:
  - type: article
    title: "RoB 2: a revised tool for assessing risk of bias in randomised trials"
    authors:
      - family-names: Sterne
        given-names: Jonathan A. C.
      - family-names: Savović
        given-names: Jelena
      - family-names: Page
        given-names: Matthew J.
      - name: "et al."
    journal: BMJ
    year: 2019
    volume: 366
    start: l4898
    doi: 10.1136/bmj.l4898
